    <title>Involution matchings, the semigroup of orientation-preserving and orientation-reversing mappings, and inverse covers of the full transformation semigroup</title>
    <updated>2019-02-07T20:18:58Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1811.04472v2" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/1811.04472v2" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>We continue the study of permutations of a finite regular semigroup that map each element to one of its inverses, providing a complete description in the case of semigroups whose idempotent generated subsemigroup is a union of groups. We show, in two ways, how to construct an involution matching on the semigroup of all transformations which either preserve or reverse orientation of a finite cycle. Finally, by way of application, we prove that finite full transformation semigroups have no cover by inverse semigroups that is closed under intersection.</summary>
